      "value": "Based on the diagnostic criteria by Dalakas (6), which include (1) muscular rigidity in the limbs and axial muscles; (2) continuous co-contraction of agonist and antagonist muscles, confirmed clinically and electrophysiologically; (3) episodic spasms; (4) absence of any other neurological diseases that could explain the symptoms; (5) and positive serology for GAD 65 (or amphiphysin) autoantibodies in the serum; the patient presented in this report met the criteria for diagnosis of SPS.",
